    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d228">

                <pb facs="0372" n="260" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg260"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum from the Russian Embassy.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial Russian Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-02-21"><hi rendition="#italic">February 21,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Having duly transmitted by cable the text of the department’s memorandum of
                    February 8 and 14, the Russian ambassador is now instructed to request of the
                    honorable the Secretary of State to be placed in possession of the conditions of
                    the contract for the Chicnchow-Aigun Railroad for transmission by cable to St.
                    Petersburg, as it is necessary for the Imperial Russian Government to be fully
                    and correctly informed on this matter in order to be able to decide the question
                    of whether Russia could, and on what conditions, participate in the said
                    enterprise.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
